<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Seosan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Seosan is a city in South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chungcheong-province">Chungcheong Province</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-korea">South Korea</a>, on the Taean peninsula facing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yellow-sea">Yellow Sea</a>. Near it is the Rock-carved Buddha Triad of Seosan, carved into a cliff in the late Baekje period, around the early seventh century, and known for the warm smiles of its figures. The triad is a National Treasure of South <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> and lay on an old route between Baekje and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/seosan.jpg" alt="Seosan" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jangg8962 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Seosan_montage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
